From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Oliver Sargison <sargo@sargo.cc>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 13:08:31 +1300
Subject: [PATCH 48/48] Plutonium: a dock slot holds one window or tab

A slot used to claim whatever fit its description: a site slot every tab
whose address started with its prefix, an app slot every window of the app
in its scope, cycling through several. Now it holds the one put in it: that
window or tab carries the slot's tag (t3:dock/<slot id>) beside its scope's,
and a press, the button's state and the panel tab's number all find it by
the two tags, wherever the tab browses. With nothing found, the press opens
a tab of the site or starts the app and tags what that made: for an app, the
new window of the process started (or of the app in the scope), not any new
window.

Assigning a tab or window moves the slot to it (what the slot held in that
scope loses the tag); changing a slot's scope retags only what it holds; a
tab a docked tab opens drops the inherited slot tag. The slot keeps its id
while it names the same app or site. The editor loses "Tabs start with";
stored slots get an id and lose their prefix.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
